deployed: 2026-05-12T14:00:00Z · v1.0.77 (THE root cause — stop
_wAttachPaneDrag clobbering canonical pane IDs.

After v1.0.60-76 telemetry, traced the actual issue back to
TWO conflicting taggers racing on .crTerm-pane elements:

  · v1.0.60 IIFE tagPanes() (at boot+0) assigns canonical paneIds
    like 'solPrice', 'solTopTokens', 'cexFunding'.
  · _wAttachPaneDrag at line 31065 (at boot+250) UNCONDITIONALLY
    overwrites with ordinals: 'crTermViewSolana.0',
    'crTermViewSolana.1', etc.

The latter wins because it runs later. End state: every Solana
+ CEX pane carried an ordinal id, not a canonical one. This
single bug caused two reported symptoms:

  · "Solana tab still shows mock data" — refreshers do
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-pane-id="solPrice"]'),
    find nothing (because the real attribute says
    'crTermViewSolana.0'), early-return.
  · "All widget configs show 'built-in pane'" — pinned widget
    sourceId was 'crTermViewSolana.0', schema lookup tried
    _CR_PANE_SCHEMAS['pane:crTermViewSolana.0'] (does not
    exist), fell back to the generic 'pane' note.

THE FIX
  · _wAttachPaneDrag now preserves existing data-pane-id and
    only stamps an ordinal when the pane has NO id. Canonical
    ids set by v1.0.60 are preserved.
  · tagPanes() upgrades ordinal IDs to canonical when it sees
    them. If _wAttachPaneDrag ever wins the race, the next
    tagPanes call (boot+3s, +8s, tab click, win-terminal
    MutationObserver) fixes it.

After this patch, the canonical id is stable across all races.
Refreshers find their bodies, gear config opens the right
schema, MutationObserver/force-tick paths work as designed.

Combined with v1.0.76 (visible body status on warn), the
Solana tab will:
