  · Browser cached the old HTML (user needs hard reload)
  · IIFE never reached due to upstream throw in the same 2.2MB
    <script> block
  · Refreshers fire but Birdeye/GoldRush all return errors silently
    (only header chip changes, body stays on mock HTML)

v1.0.75 surfaces all three with concrete telemetry the user can read
in DevTools.

DIAGNOSTIC HARNESS (window._crTermDiag)
  · iifeReached         — timestamp when the IIFE evaluated. If
                          missing, the IIFE never ran.
  · bootRan             — timestamp when _boot fired. If iifeReached
                          is set but bootRan is null, DOMContentLoaded
                          never fired (impossible-ish) OR the IIFE
                          itself threw before registering _boot.
  · tagPanesCalls       — count of tagPanes() invocations. Should
                          be ≥ 1 after boot + ≥ 4 after opening
                          Terminal + clicking the 4 tabs.
  · panesTagged         — map of paneId → tag count. Should contain
                          18 entries (9 Solana + 9 CEX). Any
                          UNMAPPED:* entries surface header text
                          that didn't match PANE_ID_MAP.
  · refresherCalls      — map of paneId → { calls, ok, fail,
                          lastErr, lastStatus }. Inspect to see
                          which refreshers are succeeding vs failing
                          and why.
  · forceTickCalls      — count of _forceTickForVisiblePanes runs.
  · lastForceTick       — { t, fired, noBody }. fired=N means N
                          refreshers actually ran; noBody=N means
                          N had no tagged body in the DOM.
  · obsHookInstalled    — timestamp when the MutationObserver
                          attached to #win-terminal. "NO
                          #win-terminal" means the element wasn\'t
                          in the DOM at hook time.

HOW TO USE
  1. Hard-reload (Cmd+Shift+R)
  2. Open DevTools → Console
  3. Look for [crTerm] log lines printed by the IIFE
  4. Run: console.dir(window._crTermDiag)
  5. Send me the output — every failure mode is now telemetered.

VISIBLE STATUS PAINTING
  Failed refreshers no longer just change the header chip — they
  now paint a STATUS MESSAGE into the pane body too. So instead
  of "old mock HTML + offline chip" you see:
    "Birdeye returned HTTP 401. Add a Birdeye API key:
     Token Terminal → ⚙ Settings."
  or
    "Network error: Failed to fetch. Retrying in next tick."
  Mock HTML can no longer be confused with stale-live state.

OTHER FIXES IN THIS PATCH
  · _BIRD_HEADERS reads localStorage.cr_birdeye_key_v1 the same
    way window.crBirdeye does. Was checking
    window.crBirdeye._key which is never set, so the X-API-KEY
    header was never being sent even when a key was configured.)

